# Copy to `.env.local` — Expo loads it automatically and `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` vars
# are inlined into the JS bundle at build time.
#
# Anything NOT prefixed with EXPO_PUBLIC_ is unavailable to the app at runtime.
# Never put a secret (API key, service token) in this file: everything that
# reaches the bundle is readable by anyone who downloads the app.

# OPTIONAL. The app is fully usable with this unset — the diary lives in a
# local SQLite database and needs no server. Set it only when you have a
# backend to sync with; without it, account sign-in reports that accounts are
# unavailable in this build, and everything else works exactly as before.
#
# Android emulator reaches the host machine at 10.0.2.2, not localhost;
# `src/lib/env.ts` rewrites that automatically.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Optional: request timeout in milliseconds (defaults to 15000).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# OPTIONAL. Gates the Google sign-in button — it's hidden/unavailable until
# this is set. Obtain it from Google Cloud Console (an OAuth 2.0 Web client
# ID, used so `GoogleSignin.configure()` can return an `idToken`).
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=your-web-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# OPTIONAL. Needed for the native iOS Google sign-in flow — separate from
# the web client ID above. Also obtained from Google Cloud Console (an
# OAuth 2.0 iOS client ID). Android does not need this.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=your-ios-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

# OPTIONAL, and NOT prefixed EXPO_PUBLIC_ — it's build-config-only, read in
# `app.config.ts`, not at runtime. The reversed form of the iOS OAuth client
# ID above, used to register the URL scheme Google sign-in redirects back
# into (e.g. com.googleusercontent.apps.1234567890-abc). A build works
# without it, using a syntactically-valid placeholder, but Google sign-in on
# iOS won't function until it's set to the real value.
# GOOGLE_IOS_URL_SCHEME=com.googleusercontent.apps.1234567890-abc
